manufactured and proposes a typology for such rings. Within that broader study, 
the so‑called Ring of Nestor is treated as a notable example, and its imagery is
discussed in relation to Egyptian iconography. The work also references Arthur 
Evans’s study \"The Ring of Nestor: A Glimpse into the Minoan After‑world,\" 
