"attempt": 1, "status": "succeeded"}, {"id": "20260628000951112904_c65729b3", 
"type": "Document", "source_id": "20260628000950923068_b91158ae", "text": "This 
Hesperia article \"The Lord of the Gold Rings\" by Jack L. Davis (2016) 
discusses the 2015 discovery of the \"Griffin Warrior\" grave near the Palace of
Nestor at Pylos. The grave, dated to Late Helladic IIA (roughly 1450–1400 BCE), 
contained hundreds of grave goods including four gold signet rings decorated 
with Minoan ritual scenes. The article describes the excavation context and 
analyzes the iconography and cultural significance of these gold rings for the 
Mycenaeans, emphasizing that many of the grave goods were manufactured in the 
Minoan world and reflect strong cultural connections between Pylos and Crete."},
